# Valgrind suppressions for poc's conservative garbage collector, beyond
# polibfyaml's test/poc-gc.supp, which make valgrind also uses.
#
# GarbageCollectedHeap.Collect scans every word of the machine stack for
# things that look like heap pointers, including words that were never
# written.  polibfyaml's file suppresses the uninitialised-value errors
# that raises in MarkCandidate.  This program's bigger frames also hand
# such a word on to the mark stack when it happens to point into a
# block, and DrainMarkStack then traces from it: "Use of uninitialised
# value of size 8" with DrainMarkStack as the top frame, which
# --track-origins=yes traces to "a stack allocation" in a frame of the
# program (Besm2Grid.ProcessEntity, for enyon-boase-2e.yaml; confirmed
# 2026-10-05, poc 0.2.0).  That is how a conservative collector works,
# not a bug in the program.
#
# Only that error kind, and only when that function is the top frame.

{
   poc-gc-drainmarkstack-value8
   Memcheck:Value8
   fun:GarbageCollectedHeap.DrainMarkStack
}
